WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.692 --> 00:00:01.525
- I was...

00:00:01.525 --> 00:00:03.380
When I was like, I don't know, 2006.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.830
I don't know what year, I
mean, how old exactly I was

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.740
but I jumped off the Mount
Vernon bridge in San Bernardino.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:09.780
You know where the Metrolink is?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.964
You know the Metrolink,
the Mount Vernon bridge?

00:00:11.964 --> 00:00:13.066
The Santa Fe bridge?

00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:14.320
I jumped off that bridge.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.003
It's a 40 foot drop.

00:00:17.154 --> 00:00:19.458
You know what I mean?

00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:20.930
This is the end result from me jumping

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.393
off the Mount Vernon bridge.

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:24.421
There it is.

00:00:25.528 --> 00:00:26.361
See it?

00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:30.426
It's like a star.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.750
A rock went through my head right here.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.630
I could stick this much of my finger

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:37.463
through my head.

00:00:37.463 --> 00:00:38.790
- [Mark] You're kidding.
- Yeah.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:39.623
My back caved in right here

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:41.977
because I hit the railroad tracks.

00:00:41.977 --> 00:00:44.880
I hit the railroad tracks,
a rock went through my head,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.453
dislocated my collarbone
and I talk like this now.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:49.303
You know what I mean?

00:00:49.303 --> 00:00:51.670
I was in a coma for about 6 months.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.930
They told me that I wouldn't have kids,

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.986
I might not be able to walk, you know.

00:00:55.986 --> 00:00:58.150
They told me a lot of things

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:01.870
and I have three beautiful
kids after the fact,

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.670
you know what I mean?

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.131
- [Mark] All right, Florencia.

00:01:19.131 --> 00:01:21.044
Florencia, where are you from originally?

00:01:21.044 --> 00:01:22.717
- I'm originally from Arizona

00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:23.550
- [Mark] Arizona?

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.550
- San Carlos

00:01:25.397 --> 00:01:27.645
- [Mark] And how long you've been here?

00:01:27.645 --> 00:01:28.728
- Since 2002.

00:01:31.113 --> 00:01:33.042
- [Mark] So 17 years?

00:01:33.042 --> 00:01:34.174
- Yeah.

00:01:34.174 --> 00:01:35.841
- [Mark] And what...

00:01:37.007 --> 00:01:38.235
tell me about your family.

00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:39.112
Do you live with...

00:01:39.112 --> 00:01:42.279
- See my mom she was a beautiful lady.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:47.000
I mean, I didn't spend
too much time with her.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.650
My mom seven months pregnant with me,

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.647
she got two life sentences.

00:01:50.647 --> 00:01:51.606
- [Mark] She what?

00:01:51.606 --> 00:01:54.240
- She got two life sentences
seven months pregnant with me.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.300
- [Mark] Two life sentences?

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.133
- Yeah.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.234
So my mom had me in prison.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:01.660
I mean and I didn't know her growing up.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.733
She never reached out to me growing up.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.410
At the time of my mom was incarcerated,

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.520
well conviction,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.700
her and my dad both got convicted.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.650
My dad got convicted of a lesser charge

00:02:15.527 --> 00:02:18.350
with aiding and abetting and
accessory after the fact.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:22.390
And my mom was the one
who was the main person.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.100
They gave her two life sentences.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.710
They gave my dad 13 years.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:26.816
- [Mark] This was for murder?

00:02:26.816 --> 00:02:28.498
- Two poli...

00:02:28.498 --> 00:02:30.191
My mom killed two cops.

00:02:30.191 --> 00:02:31.180
- [Mark] She killed two cops?

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.410
- Yeah, and tried to like
hide it, you know what I mean?

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.030
My dad tried to aid and abet it,

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:40.913
aid and abet and they gave him 13 years.

00:02:42.144 --> 00:02:44.090
Me growing up, my mom never wrote me,

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.550
never tried to reach out to me, nothing.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:49.300
My dad did, you know, so...

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.730
- [Mark] Where we you, who raised you?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.080
- My dad's mom.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.520
- [Mark] Your dad's mom.
- My dad's mom.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.240
And she did the best she
could, you know what I mean?

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.353
Under the circumstances there
was me and my seven brothers.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:02.630
And...

00:03:04.482 --> 00:03:07.352
she has six other kids other than my mom.

00:03:07.352 --> 00:03:08.200
You know what I mean?

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.303
So she had me, she had
a lot of grandkids and

00:03:12.605 --> 00:03:15.287
a lot of stuff to tend to other than me.

00:03:15.287 --> 00:03:16.120
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.037
- And so...

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.042
growing up, it was me
and my seven brothers

00:03:22.042 --> 00:03:24.680
in one house, which is
my mom and dad's house.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.390
My mom and dad lived on the
same block as my grandma

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.880
in the same street just one block away.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.675
We were on the same street.

00:03:31.675 --> 00:03:34.050
So we, me and my brothers lived down

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.150
in my mom and dad's house

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.570
and my grandma tend to us

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.440
I mean, from visiting
and making sure we ate

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.333
and clean clothes for school.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.590
- She was there I mean,
tucking me in at night,

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:50.823
reading me bedtime stories,
making sure nobody hurt me.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:55.010
Then when I was thirteen, my
dad came home from prison,

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.497
and she was like, "Oh, your
dad is home," know what I mean?

00:03:57.497 --> 00:04:00.367
"Now you guys will be okay."

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.242
Well, me not knowing my mom at the time

00:04:04.242 --> 00:04:06.907
and me being the youngest, I asked him,

00:04:06.907 --> 00:04:08.000
"Do I look like my mom?"

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.560
I'm not knowing.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.130
And one thing led to another

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:14.931
and he started to touch me
the way no father should.

00:04:14.931 --> 00:04:16.913
You know what I mean?

00:04:16.913 --> 00:04:21.800
And I was looking for
something to get him off me,

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.617
you know what I mean?

00:04:23.617 --> 00:04:25.660
And he wouldn't stop.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.290
And the more I stabbed
him, he didn't stop.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:33.290
He penetrated me until
seven stab wounds later.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.476
He penetrated me the whole
way through every stab wound,

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:38.904
I stabbed him seven different times.

00:04:38.904 --> 00:04:39.737
- [Mark] With what?

00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:44.100
- I stabbed him with
a steak knife at that.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.516
- [Mark] You were stabbing
him with a steak knife.

00:04:45.516 --> 00:04:47.338
- I made him a steak dinner.

00:04:47.338 --> 00:04:49.883
That's what he wanted because
he just came home from prison.

00:04:49.883 --> 00:04:50.810
I mean, that's my daddy.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.046
- [Mark] He's having intercourse with you

00:04:53.046 --> 00:04:54.810
while you're stabbing him?

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:55.643
- Yeah.

00:04:55.643 --> 00:04:58.228
And he penetrated the whole way through.

00:04:58.228 --> 00:05:00.640
I mean, "I'm like wait a
minute I'm your daughter,

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.680
you need to get off me."

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:05.885
Well, he took a shit on himself

00:05:05.885 --> 00:05:08.890
and immediately started coughing blood.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.770
And he's like, " Oh shit,
you're my daughter."

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.330
You know what I mean?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.860
I can't say that

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:15.693
he didn't know it was me,

00:05:15.693 --> 00:05:17.187
I can't say he didn't know it was me.

00:05:17.187 --> 00:05:20.900
I only asked a few questions to escalate

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.770
or to arouse a few things in him that,

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:26.660
I don't know, but...

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:34.533
When he died, I just pushed him off me,

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:35.366
you know what I mean?

00:05:35.366 --> 00:05:38.720
Jumped in the shower,
grabbed some ice and ran.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.400
I mean, I was scared.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.800
I was thirteen.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:42.650
I didn't know what to do.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.750
- [Mark] He died right there?

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:44.583
- Yeah.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.930
Yeah.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:51.060
And because I took a shower I
washed away all the evidence,

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.480
you know what I mean?

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:57.108
Because I ran away I looked
guilty, you know what I mean?

00:05:57.108 --> 00:05:59.950
They gave me juvenile life.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.000
Juvenile life!

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.490
I mean at thirteen years old,
I was released at twenty two.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.540
You know what I mean?

00:06:10.931 --> 00:06:14.240
And that was real hard for me.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.473
My grandma told me that
the day her son died

00:06:16.473 --> 00:06:19.045
was the day her granddaughter died.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:22.820
And she meant that to the
fullest, you know what I mean?

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:25.503
To this day, she means that.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.730
I can't say I blame her.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:33.193
From a mother's point
of view I understand.

00:06:33.193 --> 00:06:35.910
Coming from a mother's
point of view I understand.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.543
From a granddaughter's point of view,

00:06:37.543 --> 00:06:41.357
I don't understand and I
don't think I ever will.

00:06:41.357 --> 00:06:44.230
But I had to come to realize
that I wasn't the sick one.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:46.820
I wasn't the one, you know,

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.050
I wasn't the one that was
messed up in the head.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.320
You know what I mean?

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:53.013
I was the one who stopped.

00:06:53.013 --> 00:06:55.380
I mean, I was the one who stopped it,

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.210
you know, because it was a family secret.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.810
I wasn't the first one
in my family he touched.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.120
You know what I mean?

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.438
I was the last one he touched.

00:07:03.438 --> 00:07:05.846
And even though I regret it
with every thing in my life,

00:07:05.846 --> 00:07:07.260
that's the only thing I regret,

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.451
because at the end of the
day he's still my dad,

00:07:09.451 --> 00:07:11.201
you know what I mean?

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:19.483
It's hard.

00:07:19.483 --> 00:07:22.113
It's a hard pill to live
with, you know what I mean?

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.970
Because it's like I took
him from my grandma,

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:30.970
me and his sisters, my
brothers, you know what I mean?

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.897
It wasn't my call to do what I did,

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.400
but I promise, I swear to
God, on everything I love,

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.597
I wasn't trying to kill
him, I really wasn't.

00:07:41.597 --> 00:07:42.847
I just wanted him off me.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:49.500
So once I was in prison, you
know a lot of time had passed.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:50.600
You know what I mean?

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.180
But in my mind, as I got out,

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:58.288
it became brand new again.

00:07:58.288 --> 00:07:59.717
You understand what I'm saying?

00:07:59.717 --> 00:08:03.050
'Cause the time I spent in
juvenile life, I spent in prison,

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:06.230
I was able to push it behind.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:09.910
From fourteen to twenty two,
I was able to push it behind.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:13.670
I mean, now that I'm out,
I'm trying to see my family,

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:14.503
you know what I mean?

00:08:14.503 --> 00:08:17.200
And I'm trying to go around like family.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.810
They're like, "We don't
want you around here."

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:20.643
You know what I mean?

00:08:20.643 --> 00:08:23.004
And I'm like, "I'm the baby,
what are you talking about?",

00:08:23.004 --> 00:08:24.101
you know what I mean?

00:08:24.101 --> 00:08:25.768
"You're all I have."

00:08:28.251 --> 00:08:30.730
You know what I mean?

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:34.333
My dad was the only son out of five girls.

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:37.131
You know what I mean?

00:08:40.879 --> 00:08:43.629
(sobbing) Sorry.

00:08:49.881 --> 00:08:52.763
I had kids, you know what I mean?

00:08:52.763 --> 00:08:54.473
I got a life, I married.

00:08:55.873 --> 00:08:58.281
My grandmother never seen my kids.

00:08:58.281 --> 00:08:59.272
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:08:59.272 --> 00:09:00.970
- My grandmother has never seen my kids.

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.620
The whole time I had them, never.

00:09:03.534 --> 00:09:08.534
I catch a case out here
on San Julian, 2010.

00:09:08.954 --> 00:09:11.367
Six females trying to jump
me, you know what I mean?

00:09:11.367 --> 00:09:12.673
Taking about what am I doing out there,

00:09:12.673 --> 00:09:13.913
you know what I mean?

00:09:13.913 --> 00:09:15.600
I'm not Black, I'm Mexican.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.469
I'm not supposed to be out there serving,

00:09:17.469 --> 00:09:18.840
you know what I mean?

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:21.130
So I stab the first one to come at me.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.350
The other five are still fighting me,

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.790
but we all separate.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.613
When we all separate, they
go their way, I go my way.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.600
But I guess sometime during that night,

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:33.937
their friend had died.

00:09:33.937 --> 00:09:38.310
And they told on me so about
five o'clock in the morning,

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:39.143
I'm getting pulled out of my tent.

00:09:39.143 --> 00:09:41.650
Taking about homicide
detectives want to talk to me.

00:09:43.162 --> 00:09:43.995
Okay...

00:09:44.901 --> 00:09:46.910
And I'm like, "Homicide detectives?

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:47.743
What are you talking about?

00:09:47.743 --> 00:09:49.817
I didn't kill anybody,"
you know what I mean?

00:09:49.817 --> 00:09:51.067
"I'm sleeping," you know what I mean?

00:09:51.067 --> 00:09:52.519
"I was in a fight, but that was it.

00:09:52.519 --> 00:09:53.960
It mean anything."

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.698
"Well, because the outcome of that fight,

00:09:56.698 --> 00:10:01.620
I mean, someone died and you're guilty.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.907
You are the suspect."

00:10:04.147 --> 00:10:05.050
"The suspect?

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.250
There's five of them, there's one of me,

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.320
how am I the suspect?"

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.791
You know what I mean?

00:10:08.791 --> 00:10:11.140
Their word against mine.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:13.990
My previous conviction from my dad.

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:16.037
Even though it shouldn't have been put up

00:10:16.037 --> 00:10:17.586
'cause it's juvenile case.

00:10:17.586 --> 00:10:19.705
Under the same proc...

00:10:19.705 --> 00:10:20.538
Under the same...

00:10:22.122 --> 00:10:23.130
same motive,

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:26.252
you know, the same kind
of act, the same...

00:10:26.252 --> 00:10:27.911
- [Mark] Yeah, very similar.

00:10:27.911 --> 00:10:31.310
- So, I took ten.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.403
I took ten at 85%.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.770
I go in, I come across my mom.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:42.183
You know what I mean and...

00:10:42.183 --> 00:10:43.560
- [Mark] You're in the
same prison with your mom.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.420
- I'm in the same prison with my mom.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.470
Now mind you, this is thirty
something years after the fact.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:49.810
You know what I mean?

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.570
And I'm like, "Why?

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:52.900
Why did you never write me?

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:53.733
What do you mean?

00:10:53.733 --> 00:10:54.566
What did I do?."

00:10:54.566 --> 00:10:55.451
You know what I mean?

00:10:55.451 --> 00:10:57.683
She was able to say she didn't know me.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.773
She didn't know how I was
going to act, how I felt,

00:11:00.773 --> 00:11:01.606
you know what I mean?

00:11:01.606 --> 00:11:02.787
But she was scared.

00:11:02.787 --> 00:11:04.423
I understand.

00:11:04.423 --> 00:11:06.260
I mean, I understand.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.093
You know what I mean?

00:11:07.093 --> 00:11:08.432
"At the same time, you're my mom,

00:11:08.432 --> 00:11:10.573
I love you, you know what I mean?

00:11:10.573 --> 00:11:13.445
I mean, it was for me as it was for you.

00:11:13.445 --> 00:11:14.710
You know what I mean?"

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:19.420
And so we get close somewhat
close during these eight years.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.898
We were able to grow a bond.

00:11:20.898 --> 00:11:22.065
- [Mark] Nice.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:26.243
- I get out December 16th.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:31.913
While I was incarcerated,

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.800
my son dies May 31st.

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:40.154
My firstborn, May 31st 2018.

00:11:40.154 --> 00:11:40.987
- [Mark] I'm so sorry.

00:11:40.987 --> 00:11:45.723
- He gets hit by a car
out in Rialto and he dies.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:51.134
And I'm like, (sobbing)

00:11:51.134 --> 00:11:53.270
you mean, no, what do you mean?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.470
That's my baby, my first
born, you know what I mean?

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.833
He's 12 years old, about to be 13.

00:11:59.591 --> 00:12:03.570
He died one day before
his birthday, he died.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:04.403
And...

00:12:07.298 --> 00:12:09.740
when I went to the funeral
because I was almost home,

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:10.573
you know what I mean?

00:12:10.573 --> 00:12:12.210
I was able to go to the funeral.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.843
My grandma, he was in the care
of my grandma when he passed.

00:12:16.698 --> 00:12:17.935
My grandmother then tells me,

00:12:17.935 --> 00:12:20.453
"Now you know what it
feels like to lose a son."

00:12:20.453 --> 00:12:24.260
When I was a kid, playing in
the front yard wasn't allowed,

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.680
you understand what I'm saying?

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:26.800
There were other kids there.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.878
My daughter tells me, she tells me,

00:12:28.878 --> 00:12:32.787
"The day my brother died
I was mad, mom, mad!"

00:12:32.787 --> 00:12:34.125
"Why were you so mad?"

00:12:34.125 --> 00:12:35.997
"Because I want to play with the kids...

00:12:35.997 --> 00:12:39.410
I want to play in the back
with the rest of the kids,

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:42.334
but grandma says we had
to stay in the front."

00:12:42.334 --> 00:12:45.449
So my daughter is telling
me this and I'm like,

00:12:45.449 --> 00:12:48.270
"What do you mean with
the rest of the kids?"

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.330
Everybody in the back, mom.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:52.717
Me and my brothers are the
only ones in the front.

00:12:52.717 --> 00:12:55.043
The play football, the
ball goes on the street.

00:12:55.043 --> 00:12:58.050
Ciroc tried to get it, but
Crip was like, "No Papas,

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:00.240
you don't want to go in the
street, Papas, no Papas."

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:02.051
He's being a big brother, you know?

00:13:02.051 --> 00:13:05.930
He goes, they say he
looks both ways, no cars,

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.690
but as soon as he grabs the ball,

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:09.550
the car comes out of nowhere.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:10.613
Boom, he dies.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:22.270
Being locked up, not
being there for my kid

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.899
like I was supposed to shows me

00:13:24.899 --> 00:13:26.334
no one is going to take care of your kids

00:13:26.334 --> 00:13:28.560
the way you're going to
take care of your kids.

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.390
You know what I mean?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:33.603
I can't see my grandma enticing
to get my son killed, no.

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.066
But when she made the statement,

00:13:37.066 --> 00:13:41.273
"Now you know what it
feels like to lose a son,"

00:13:41.273 --> 00:13:44.650
kinda makes me feel like she was,

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:46.527
she wanted something to happen.

00:13:46.527 --> 00:13:48.790
She wanted me to feel her pain.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:51.373
You understand what I'm saying?

00:13:52.862 --> 00:13:56.180
And, oh, do I feel it. (sobbing)

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:58.033
I've always felt it though.

00:13:59.541 --> 00:14:01.803
He was my dad at the end of the day.

00:14:02.915 --> 00:14:05.187
He wouldn't stop penetrating me.

00:14:05.187 --> 00:14:06.073
If he had stopped penetrating me,

00:14:06.073 --> 00:14:08.340
I would have stopped stabbing.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.990
You know what I mean?

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:18.880
So, I come home, my son dies May 31st.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.689
His birthday is June 1st.

00:14:21.689 --> 00:14:23.389
He dies a day before his birthday.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.183
I come home December.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:27.883
And I leave my mom,

00:14:27.883 --> 00:14:30.498
and I tell my mom, "I'm
going to send you...

00:14:30.498 --> 00:14:31.710
I'm going to send you boxes.

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:34.617
If you need anything, call,
let me know, I got you.

00:14:34.617 --> 00:14:35.963
But mom, I love you."

00:14:35.963 --> 00:14:37.778
You know what I mean?

00:14:37.778 --> 00:14:40.630
"I'm going to come back
and see you again."

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:44.793
And we say our goodbyes.

00:14:44.793 --> 00:14:47.870
Two months later my mom passes.

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:51.700
She got sick and she had
caught an abscess in prison.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.513
I don't know if you
know what an abscess is.

00:14:53.513 --> 00:14:56.523
It's like a boil of poison from slamming.

00:14:58.487 --> 00:15:03.014
What happened was the
boil popped from inside.

00:15:03.014 --> 00:15:05.303
It went straight to her heart,

00:15:05.303 --> 00:15:08.660
straight to her bloodstream, to her heart

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:10.060
and it killed her instantly.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:12.513
Instantly.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.620
So I get a phone call saying

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.409
my mom had just passed.

00:15:17.409 --> 00:15:18.242
(sobbing) And I'm like, "I just left her,

00:15:18.242 --> 00:15:20.270
what are you talking
about she just passed?"

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.410
You know I just left her
not even two months ago,

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.733
you know what I mean?

00:15:29.254 --> 00:15:30.729
And I was like it's okay.

00:15:30.729 --> 00:15:33.622
It's okay, she was in prison for 37 years.

00:15:33.622 --> 00:15:36.905
She gets to leave now,
you know what I mean?

00:15:36.905 --> 00:15:39.200
She don't got to be trapped
no more, you know what I mean?

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.033
She's free.

00:15:43.901 --> 00:15:47.234
(airplane passing over)

00:15:59.558 --> 00:16:02.475
(exhaling quietly)

00:16:04.559 --> 00:16:08.439
(Florencia sniffling)

00:16:08.439 --> 00:16:11.772
So, my husband, the one who had my kids

00:16:12.755 --> 00:16:15.076
before I went to prison.

00:16:15.076 --> 00:16:17.073
The one who dropped my
kids off at my grandma's.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:19.948
He feels so bad.

00:16:19.948 --> 00:16:22.707
You know, he blames himself
that he should never have

00:16:22.707 --> 00:16:23.540
taken them there.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.840
He should have just kept them
home, you know what I mean?

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:28.870
He catches a case.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:31.093
He goes to Vegas,
kidnaps two white people.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.680
He gets two first degree kidnapping,

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.749
assault with a deadly weapon,
conspiracy to commit robbery,

00:16:36.749 --> 00:16:39.090
robbery, impersonating a public officer.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:43.041
He picks up a very big case,
where they give him life.

00:16:43.041 --> 00:16:45.020
They gave him life.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:46.257
Mind you, I'm...

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.403
(counting quietly)

00:16:52.403 --> 00:16:55.903
I was six months to the gate at this time.

00:16:56.751 --> 00:16:59.630
When my husband caught life,

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:02.550
I was five months to the gate.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:06.348
I had about five months to
come home, when he caught life.

00:17:06.348 --> 00:17:09.070
When he caught life, they took the house.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.330
They, I mean...

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.370
The owner said that we
forfeit the property

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:16.106
because neither one of us
was there, we abandoned it.

00:17:16.106 --> 00:17:16.939
You know.

00:17:18.269 --> 00:17:21.990
So then they took our house
and all our belongings.

00:17:23.123 --> 00:17:27.042
Now that I come home from
prison, I come home to what?

00:17:27.042 --> 00:17:28.313
Nothing.

00:17:29.452 --> 00:17:32.390
I come home to two kids that my brother

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:36.240
has temporary custody of.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.290
You know what I mean?

00:17:38.334 --> 00:17:42.537
Temporary guardianship
because I'm in prison

00:17:42.537 --> 00:17:45.677
and my brother's in prison, I
mean my husband's in prison.

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:52.220
I get out of prison and
my son had just passed

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:54.533
and my husband went to prison.

00:17:55.392 --> 00:17:59.160
They took everything,
everything we owned was gone.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.540
And I'm like, now where do I go?

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.584
I don't want to come back

00:18:02.584 --> 00:18:04.243
because this is where everything began.

00:18:05.097 --> 00:18:08.967
And I'm like, I'm looking
and everyone is like,

00:18:08.967 --> 00:18:10.870
"No, you can't come here,
you can't come here."

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:11.703
You know what I mean?

00:18:11.703 --> 00:18:12.577
And I'm like,

00:18:12.577 --> 00:18:13.800
"I'm you guys' family.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:17.062
I mean you're all I have. (Florencia sobs)

00:18:17.062 --> 00:18:18.393
You know what I mean.

00:18:18.393 --> 00:18:20.693
I don't know nobody else but you guys.

00:18:21.936 --> 00:18:25.673
And I'm sorry for my dad, I'm sorry.

00:18:28.068 --> 00:18:30.717
What do you expect me to do?

00:18:30.717 --> 00:18:33.223
What do you expect me to do?"

00:18:33.223 --> 00:18:35.350
"No, no we just finished talking.

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:36.493
You don't come here."

00:18:40.766 --> 00:18:45.266
So, against everything I
want, I ended back down here.

00:18:48.523 --> 00:18:52.247
So I get a tent, and I make my mind.

00:18:53.205 --> 00:18:56.590
Okay, since I caught
that case in San Julian,

00:18:56.590 --> 00:19:00.100
let's not go there, let's
come to the other side.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.150
You know what I mean?

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:06.740
Anything past San Pedro
should be okay for me.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:10.879
Well, I come to 6th and
Crocker and I pitch my tent,

00:19:10.879 --> 00:19:15.879
and I instantly fall into
line with the same stuff

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:18.500
I was doing before, I got busted.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:19.789
But the only thing that changes,

00:19:19.789 --> 00:19:22.696
back then I was smocking crack real heavy,

00:19:22.696 --> 00:19:26.376
I was smoking crack cocaine you know.

00:19:26.376 --> 00:19:28.350
And I was real bad into addiction,

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.110
I would take the dope man's,

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:34.027
I would rob the dope man,
you know what I mean?

00:19:34.027 --> 00:19:36.790
I'd take his whole sack,
stick it in my mouth

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.650
and tell him look, "You
can either beat me up

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:40.250
or can wait for me to pay you."

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:41.260
The choice is yours.

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:44.150
Sometimes I'd get beat
up, sometimes they waited,

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:46.410
but I was seeing that crack
at the end of the day,

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.766
you know what I mean?

00:19:47.766 --> 00:19:52.766
And so this time coming home,
I didn't have that craving.

00:19:52.907 --> 00:19:56.770
Which I thank God for,
you know what I mean?

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.943
I could smell it, it don't tempt me.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.443
I can be around it. I don't want it.

00:20:02.443 --> 00:20:03.843
You understand what I'm saying?

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:08.850
I must have came home, I
came home from prison with

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.700
about eight bottles of crystal

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:13.853
and about five balloons, which is heroin.

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:19.430
And I came home from
prison, and I put my tent up

00:20:19.430 --> 00:20:22.173
and started with what I came home with.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:25.760
Now, mind you, I came home
from prison with this.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:26.593
You know what I mean?

00:20:26.593 --> 00:20:28.138
I didn't buy it when I got home.

00:20:28.138 --> 00:20:31.893
And you'd be surprised how
much drugs are in prison.

00:20:31.893 --> 00:20:33.863
I mean, you would be surprised.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:36.563
But...

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:39.236
so I come out here

00:20:39.236 --> 00:20:42.043
and they're like, "You
got have a block now.

00:20:42.043 --> 00:20:43.723
This is my block, this
is so and so's block,

00:20:43.723 --> 00:20:45.320
that's so and so's block.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.580
This block right here
technically on this side,

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:49.160
they don't belongs to nobody,

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.606
but across the street,
it belongs to somebody."

00:20:51.606 --> 00:20:53.629
You know I'm like, "I don't
give a fuck about none of that,

00:20:53.629 --> 00:20:54.462
you know what I mean?

00:20:54.462 --> 00:20:55.295
This is Skid Row.

00:20:55.295 --> 00:20:56.607
It's free land," you know what I mean?

00:20:56.607 --> 00:20:58.851
"Don't nobody own this
shit," you know what I mean?

00:20:58.851 --> 00:21:01.690
I would strictly go back
to that same mentality

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:03.757
when I caught my case.

00:21:03.757 --> 00:21:04.980
I'm not Mexican.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:05.813
I'm Native American.

00:21:05.813 --> 00:21:06.970
I can do what the fuck I want to do.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.370
You know what I mean?

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:12.693
And so I go with that
mentality once again.

00:21:12.693 --> 00:21:17.693
And so I'm selling the
products that I have.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:20.792
The crystal meth and the black,

00:21:20.792 --> 00:21:23.180
and all of a sudden someone tells me,

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:25.807
"By 10 o'clock tonight you
have to get off the block."

00:21:26.917 --> 00:21:27.750
"Who?

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.120
Who has to get off the block?"

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:30.953
Now, mind you,

00:21:30.953 --> 00:21:33.383
I already have my own people
who know me from the past.

00:21:33.383 --> 00:21:35.881
I already have a clientele,
you know what I mean?

00:21:35.881 --> 00:21:38.640
Things escalated real fast.

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:40.890
You understand what I'm saying?

00:21:40.890 --> 00:21:42.510
And so they were like,
"Well, 10 o'clock tonight,

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:44.777
you've got to be off the block."

00:21:44.777 --> 00:21:46.777
"You and what army is going to move me?"

00:21:47.717 --> 00:21:50.117
"Oh, well, this is such and
such and such and such."

00:21:50.117 --> 00:21:51.303
"Okay.

00:21:51.303 --> 00:21:53.413
I'm from the same place you're from.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:56.299
I ain't going nowhere.

00:21:56.299 --> 00:22:01.208
You mean you sell black
and any crack, okay.

00:22:01.208 --> 00:22:04.530
At the time, my black had already sold,

00:22:04.530 --> 00:22:06.200
so I just had the crystal meth.

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:08.810
I told them, "I'm not
selling anything but crystal,

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:11.660
so, technically, I'm not
interfering with your money,

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:14.460
so, technically, you can't
kick me off the block.

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.678
Especially if like we're
not from the same set,

00:22:17.678 --> 00:22:21.245
but we're from the same
neighborhood, you know what I mean?"

00:22:21.245 --> 00:22:24.099
And so he's like, "No,
I don't give a fuck.

00:22:24.099 --> 00:22:26.147
You still got to get off the block."

00:22:26.147 --> 00:22:27.187
"Okay, bet."

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:32.667
I go to his big, the person
higher than him and I'm like,

00:22:32.667 --> 00:22:34.532
"Man look you know me.

00:22:34.532 --> 00:22:36.590
You already know I'm
with all the business,

00:22:36.590 --> 00:22:37.423
you know what I mean?

00:22:37.423 --> 00:22:38.256
Like I don't give a fuck,
you know what I mean,

00:22:38.256 --> 00:22:39.521
I ain't got no sense.

00:22:39.521 --> 00:22:40.570
You know what I mean?

00:22:40.570 --> 00:22:43.440
And whatever, let's have
a stand off if we have to,

00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:44.273
I don't care.

00:22:44.273 --> 00:22:45.106
I'm not moving.

00:22:45.106 --> 00:22:46.745
It's my neighborhood, your neighborhood.

00:22:46.745 --> 00:22:49.360
I'm not moving, you know what I mean?"

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:51.725
And I....

00:22:51.725 --> 00:22:55.073
The way I approached,
the way I came at him.

00:22:55.073 --> 00:22:58.075
"This is where your money's at,

00:22:58.075 --> 00:23:01.009
the hard and the black.

00:23:01.009 --> 00:23:03.358
I'm not interfering with that.

00:23:03.358 --> 00:23:05.360
I'm not, I have nothing to do with that.

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:07.040
I'm selling a whole different product

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:09.320
that you don't even mess with.

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:11.460
So if I'm not interfering with your money,

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:14.140
technically you can't
kick them off the block.

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:16.919
Especially if I'm a hustler
just like you're a hustler,

00:23:16.919 --> 00:23:18.670
you know what I mean?"

00:23:18.670 --> 00:23:23.430
So when I went that route, it
gave me something to stand on,

00:23:23.430 --> 00:23:24.420
you know what I mean?

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.275
Well, he was like, "Wow, you're right.

00:23:26.275 --> 00:23:30.714
Since I don't serve that,
wherever I serve, you're free,

00:23:30.714 --> 00:23:32.647
you're welcome to."

00:23:32.647 --> 00:23:35.008
You know what I mean?

00:23:35.008 --> 00:23:38.310
So now it's like giving
me a key, like, "here,"

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:40.160
you know what I mean,
"This is, this is all you.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:41.393
This is your...

00:23:41.393 --> 00:23:43.130
This is your domain.

00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:44.893
Whatcha going to do with it?"

00:23:44.893 --> 00:23:48.010
So, that starts to happen.

00:23:48.010 --> 00:23:50.580
Now, all of a sudden
my daughter gets sick.

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:51.413
You know what I mean?

00:23:51.413 --> 00:23:52.544
My second to the oldest.

00:23:52.544 --> 00:23:53.377
- [Mark] How old is she?

00:23:53.377 --> 00:23:54.510
- She's seven.

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:56.557
She passed away Monday.

00:23:56.557 --> 00:23:59.120
She had a bump on her arm.

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:00.940
- [Mark] When did your daughter pass away?

00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:02.074
- Monday.

00:24:02.074 --> 00:24:04.148
- [Mark] Last week?
- Yes.

00:24:04.148 --> 00:24:07.477
- [Mark] How old?
- Seven, you know what I mean?

00:24:07.477 --> 00:24:10.293
She was only in the
hospital for two months.

00:24:11.199 --> 00:24:13.470
She had a lump in her arm.

00:24:14.420 --> 00:24:16.770
And they went in and they checked it

00:24:16.770 --> 00:24:18.920
and it kept positive for cancer.

00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:20.800
They went in to remove
it, you know what I mean?

00:24:20.800 --> 00:24:23.260
As quickly as possible before spreads.

00:24:23.260 --> 00:24:25.190
But once they cut her open,

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:27.647
once they cut it open a
it (imitates spraying),

00:24:28.837 --> 00:24:31.270
it spread it rapidly.

00:24:31.270 --> 00:24:33.260
You understand what I'm saying?

00:24:33.260 --> 00:24:36.360
Where like started having
like minor like seizures

00:24:36.360 --> 00:24:38.520
and minor strokes, you know?

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:40.370
And then she had a major stroke

00:24:40.370 --> 00:24:43.270
and she was in a coma for about a week.

00:24:43.270 --> 00:24:44.610
And they're like, "It's not looking good,

00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:46.210
you know what I mean, maybe
we should put the plug."

00:24:46.210 --> 00:24:47.930
And I'm like, "No," you know mean?

00:24:47.930 --> 00:24:48.763
No.

00:24:48.763 --> 00:24:49.596
You mean like...

00:24:50.910 --> 00:24:53.511
But it's...

00:24:53.511 --> 00:24:55.273
It's not easy.

00:24:56.303 --> 00:25:00.293
You know I'm not supposed to bury my kids.

00:25:02.070 --> 00:25:04.160
You know, I'm not.

00:25:04.160 --> 00:25:06.690
My kids are supposed to bury me.

00:25:06.690 --> 00:25:08.440
You know what I mean?

00:25:09.340 --> 00:25:11.773
I buried my first one last year.

00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:15.150
I buried my mom a few months ago.

00:25:15.150 --> 00:25:19.953
Now I'm, on Wednesday, I'll
be burying my daughter.

00:25:21.910 --> 00:25:23.790
I had to pull the plug.

00:25:23.790 --> 00:25:26.790
She was in hospital for two
months at Loma Linda University.

00:25:28.070 --> 00:25:30.757
85% brain dead, you know.

00:25:33.400 --> 00:25:36.070
I gave up the dope scene,
I gave up everything.

00:25:36.070 --> 00:25:36.960
You know what I mean?

00:25:36.960 --> 00:25:38.427
I had to make a decision.

00:25:38.427 --> 00:25:39.600
What was more important?

00:25:39.600 --> 00:25:43.731
The block and trying to get
it together or my daughter?

00:25:43.731 --> 00:25:48.731
And I had to do what
was best for my family.

00:25:48.770 --> 00:25:49.603
You know what I mean?

00:25:49.603 --> 00:25:50.860
And I had to let everything go.

00:25:50.860 --> 00:25:53.486
You know what I mean?

00:25:53.486 --> 00:25:57.967
It's like, please don't
take her, please take her.

00:26:07.628 --> 00:26:11.533
Pulling the plug on a child is so hard,

00:26:13.510 --> 00:26:16.590
because in the back of your
mind, you tell yourself,

00:26:16.590 --> 00:26:17.423
"What if?

00:26:18.649 --> 00:26:21.590
But what if none of that happens?

00:26:21.590 --> 00:26:23.920
What if she's going to be fine?

00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:27.377
Who are they to say
what's going to happen?"

00:26:27.377 --> 00:26:30.283
The minute they open it, opened her up,

00:26:30.283 --> 00:26:32.963
everything happened so fast.

00:26:43.178 --> 00:26:46.178
(Florencia sobbing)

00:26:52.571 --> 00:26:55.463
I hd my family even bashing,

00:26:55.463 --> 00:26:57.700
"Quit being selfish, quit being selfish.

00:26:57.700 --> 00:26:59.190
You need to let her go.

00:26:59.190 --> 00:27:00.540
You're just holding onto something

00:27:00.540 --> 00:27:02.087
that's never going to be there again."

00:27:02.087 --> 00:27:04.630
And I'm like, "How do we know?"

00:27:04.630 --> 00:27:07.400
You know, "We can't
pull the plug, we can't.

00:27:07.400 --> 00:27:09.350
We have to give her a fighting chance."

00:27:13.376 --> 00:27:15.433
(Florencia sobbing)

00:27:15.433 --> 00:27:16.266
And...

00:27:18.532 --> 00:27:22.680
When they check, she's
85% brain dead and...

00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:26.243
now I'm signing papers
saying that whatever happens

00:27:26.243 --> 00:27:29.010
at this point saying,

00:27:29.010 --> 00:27:31.313
I'm going against the
doctor's recommendation.

00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:35.490
I have to sign papers saying

00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:39.160
that whatever happens to my daughter,

00:27:39.160 --> 00:27:40.390
I can't blame the hospital.

00:27:40.390 --> 00:27:42.140
You understand what I'm saying?

00:27:42.140 --> 00:27:45.160
Because I'm going against
what the doctors recommended,

00:27:45.160 --> 00:27:48.013
and the doctors recommend
pulling the plug.

00:27:48.013 --> 00:27:48.846
You know what I mean?

00:27:48.846 --> 00:27:51.168
And I'm like, "No," you
know what I mean, "No."

00:27:51.168 --> 00:27:52.001
(Florencia sobbing)

00:27:52.001 --> 00:27:54.750
And so, I have to sign a paper saying

00:27:54.750 --> 00:27:59.367
I take full responsibility of
whatever happens after this.

00:28:04.850 --> 00:28:07.530
This is my daughter, this is my child.

00:28:07.530 --> 00:28:10.590
This is somebody I birthed,
you know what I mean?

00:28:10.590 --> 00:28:14.060
How am I going to pull
the plug so she can die?

00:28:14.060 --> 00:28:15.260
You know what I mean?

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:17.160
We don't know what the doctor's saying.

00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:18.970
They told me I would never walk again,

00:28:18.970 --> 00:28:19.990
I won't ever have kids.

00:28:19.990 --> 00:28:21.905
I have three beautiful
kids, you know what I mean?

00:28:21.905 --> 00:28:24.629
I already buried one now
I'm burying another one.

00:28:24.629 --> 00:28:27.361
I only have one left and it's like,

00:28:27.361 --> 00:28:29.694
"What do you want me to do?"

00:28:31.208 --> 00:28:34.602
I'm only human, I'm not strong.

00:28:34.602 --> 00:28:36.435
I might look strong...

00:28:37.726 --> 00:28:41.277
(sobbing) I'm not that
strong for all of this.

00:28:41.277 --> 00:28:43.048
And they say God will never give you

00:28:43.048 --> 00:28:45.215
anything you can't handle.

00:28:49.762 --> 00:28:52.762
(Florencia sobbing)

